From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kvmem): wire llama-kvmem-server into the tree, links
 clean on gfx1030

The adapter was compiled but unreachable: llama-server has no kvmem code at
all, and g_kvmem_params is only ever written by llama_kvmem_set_params(),
which only the KVMem tools call. Add their targets here (upstream declares
them in its superproject root, but this tree IS the llama.cpp tree):

  tools/kvmem/CMakeLists.txt   llama-kvmem-server + llama-kvmem-cli
  tools/CMakeLists.txt         add_subdirectory(kvmem) under LLAMA_KVMEM

Two base-drift fixes were needed to get there:

  * kvmem must be STATIC. This tree builds ggml/llama-common shared, so the
    vendored add_library(kvmem ...) produced kvmem.dll with an empty export
    table (no dllexport anywhere in libkvmem) and every kvmem:: symbol failed
    to link into llama.dll. Upstream forces BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF on Windows.

  * kvmem-vision.cpp called mtmd_helper_init_opt_default(), which does not
    exist in this tree: process_mtmd_prompt() is still the older
    bool is_placeholder overload. Pass false (same "real tokens" semantics)
    and include mtmd-helper.h explicitly, since this tree's server-common.h
    does not re-export it the way the newer one does.

Build result, build-hip, ROCm 7.1 / gfx1030:

  llama-server.exe        NINJA_RC=0   282/282 targets
  llama-kvmem-server.exe  NINJA_RC=0   1.86 MB

llama-kvmem-server --help prints the full --kvmem* surface (budget,
block-tokens, gen-reserve, method, query-*, mtp-state, gpu-ratio, cpu-gb,
nvme-*, kv-dtype, -ctk/-ctv) and defaults to --kvmem on.

Known gap, documented in docs/kvmem/FUSION-NOTES.md: kvmem_parse_cache_type()
accepts only f16/f32/q8_0/q5_0/q4_0, so PrismML turbo3/turbo4 cannot be
selected for the KV cache in the fused server yet.

Also add docs/kvmem/FUSION-NOTES.md: the vendoring inventory, the 14-hunk
conflict table, the HIP compat layer, the three Windows build traps and the
exact build command.
