+# KVMem fusion notes
+
+How KVMem's tiered KV memory was fused into this PrismML + TurboQuant tree, what
+had to be adapted, and how to build it on this host.
+
+- Upstream: `https://github.com/kvmem/kvmem-llama.cpp` @ `485824c`, VERSION `0.16.0-rc3`
+- Vendored base: the patch is a cumulative diff against llama.cpp `b81c99b479d4c24e5eeca10de99032ebd343ef8f`
+- Branch: `kvmem-fusion`, started from `fusion-turboquant-on-prism` @ `5f5960b`
+
+KVMem is **not a fork**. It is an out-of-tree adapter: `llama.cpp` upstream is a
+submodule that the patch is applied to, and the adapter sources live beside it.
+The CMake contract is `-DLLAMA_KVMEM=ON -DLLAMA_KVMEM_ROOT=<kvmem root>`, where
+the root provides both `src/adapter/` and `kvmem/`.
+
+## What was brought in
+
+| Path | Contents |
+|---|---|
+| `src/adapter/` | 16 files, the integration layer. `llama-memory-kvmem.cpp` (143 KB) is the tiered store; `-mtp` and `-hybrid` are the MTP and hybrid-SSM variants |
+| `kvmem/` | Host-only portable library (`libkvmem`): store, runtime, raw store, RoPE. NVMe tier is POSIX-only and auto-disables on Windows |
+| `patches/kvmem/` | The upstream patch plus its historical predecessors, kept for provenance |
+| `tools/kvmem/` | KVMem's own server/CLI (`llama-kvmem-server.cpp`, `llama-kvmem-cli.cpp`), the KVMem-only headers and the lightweight web UI. **These are the only entry point to the adapter** — see below |
+| `tests/kvmem/`, `docs/kvmem/` | Upstream tests and design/milestone docs |
+
+## Patch replay
+
+`patches/kvmem/llama-kvmem-current.patch` touches 38 files (+734 / -152) and does
+**not** contain the adapter sources — those are a straight copy. 29 hunks applied
+clean; 14 collided with the prism branch and were resolved by hand.
+
+| File | Conflict | Resolution |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ggml/include/ggml.h` | clean | adds `GGML_OP_GATED_DELTA_NET_RECORD` |
+| `ggml/src/ggml.c` | name/symbol tables | added the two array entries; `GGML_OP_COUNT` had to go to **103**, because prism already carries `GGML_OP_TURBO_WHT` (the patch expected 102) |
+| `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c` | 2 of 3 hunks | added the dispatch cases in the `n_tasks` and `ggml_graph_plan` switches |
+| `ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu` | 1 case | added the case to `ggml_cuda_supports_op`, sharing the `src[6]` guard with `GATED_DELTA_NET` |
+| `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp` | `K >= 1` / `K > 1` | `K >= 0` and `K != 1`: the RECORD op (K == 0) has no state output, so it uses the scratch slot |
+| `ggml/src/ggml-cuda/gated_delta_net.cu` | 2 hunks | guarded `state += state_out_offset` with `K > 0` so the pointer stays in bounds for RECORD. **Deliberately skipped** the second hunk's cosmetic refactor into `gdn_delta_f32`/`gdn_update_f32` — prism's kernel is column-sharded (`s_shard[c][r]`) and the upstream helper shape does not fit without rewriting it for no functional gain |
+| `src/llama-kv-cells.h` | field | added `llama_pos logical_pos = -1` to `llama_kv_cell_ext` |
+| `src/llama-kv-cache.cpp` | `ext` population | prism only sets `ext` for 2D positions. Widened the condition to `is_pos_2d() \|\| token \|\| logical_pos` and populate `ext.logical_pos` from `ubatch.logical_pos` (falling back to `pos`). KVMem reads this back as the cache row identity, so it must be written on every token batch |
+| `src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp` | 4 hunks | replay scratch sizing (`REPLAY_COUNT` extra tensor rows when `replay`), `replay_l` resize, the five `gdn_record_*` tensors per layer, and `this->n_rs_seq` in the size log |
+| `src/models/delta-net-base.cpp` | 1 hunk | replay-aware `K = has_replay() ? (is_recording() ? 0 : 1) : n_rs_seq + 1`, the k/v/g/b record copies, and `K > 0` guards on the fused-node registration |
+
+## PrismML divergences fixed
+
+- **`llama_kv_cache` lost its `name_tag` parameter.** Upstream (and KVMem, which
+  builds a *second* cache and passes `"kvmem-mtp"`) rely on it so two caches in one
+  model do not collide on `cache_k_l0`. Restored as a defaulted trailing
+  `const char * name_tag = ""`, with naming back to `cache_%sk_l%d`.
+- **No PLE conv state / different `llama_memory_recurrent` shape.** The vendored
+  hunks assumed `hparams.ple_conv_state()`; prism has no PLE, so the scratch sizing
+  is `(2u + (replay ? REPLAY_COUNT : 0)) * n_layer * overhead`.
+
+## The stock server cannot switch KVMem on
+
+`src/llama-model.cpp` calls `llama_memory_kvmem_maybe_create()`, but that starts
+with `if (!g_kvmem_params.enabled) return nullptr;` — and `g_kvmem_params` is only
+ever written by `llama_kvmem_set_params()`, which **no llama.cpp tool calls**.
+`tools/server/` has zero `kvmem` references; the `--kvmem*` flags are parsed by a
+hand-rolled parser inside `tools/kvmem/llama-kvmem-server.cpp`. So with the stock
+`llama-server` the adapter is compiled in and dead.
+
+Upstream declares `llama-kvmem-server` / `llama-kvmem-cli` in its *superproject*
+root, where `llama.cpp` is a subdirectory. Here the fusion tree **is** the
+llama.cpp tree, so `tools/kvmem/CMakeLists.txt` was added and hooked into
+`tools/CMakeLists.txt` under `if (LLAMA_KVMEM)`.
+
+| Target | Sources | Links |
+|---|---|---|
+| `llama-kvmem-server` | `llama-kvmem-server.cpp`, `kvmem-spec.cpp`, `kvmem-vision.cpp`, `tools/server/server-common.cpp` | `llama llama-common cpp-httplib mtmd` |
+| `llama-kvmem-cli` | `llama-kvmem-cli.cpp`, `kvmem-spec.cpp` | `llama llama-common` |
+
+Verified surface (`llama-kvmem-server --help`): `--kvmem` / `--no-kvmem`
+(**default on**), `--kvmem-budget`, `--kvmem-block-tokens`, `--kvmem-sink-tokens`,
+`--kvmem-gen-reserve`, `--kvmem-recent-tokens`, `--kvmem-method`,
+`--kvmem-query-*`, `--kvmem-mtp-state`, `--kvmem-gpu-ratio`, `--kvmem-cpu-gb`,
+`--kvmem-nvme-gb|dir`, `--kvmem-harvest-v`, `--kvmem-raw-k-nvme`, `--kv-dtype`,
+`-ctk/-ctv`, `--spec-type draft-mtp`, `--spec-draft-n-max`.
+
+## Base drift (the tree is 437 commits behind)
+
+Two things assumed by the vendored sources exist only in the pinned base
+`b81c99b`, not here:
+
+1. **`kvmem/CMakeLists.txt` had to go `STATIC`.** Upstream sets
+   `BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF` on Windows; this tree builds ggml/llama-common shared,
+   so `add_library(kvmem ...)` produced `kvmem.dll` with an **empty export table**
+   (libkvmem carries no `__declspec(dllexport)`), and every `kvmem::` symbol failed
+   to link into `llama.dll`. Static is also what upstream effectively gets on Linux.
+2. **`tools/kvmem/kvmem-vision.cpp`.** Newer `process_mtmd_prompt()` takes an
+   `mtmd_helper_init_opt` object; this tree still takes `bool is_placeholder`, so
+   `mtmd_helper_init_opt_default()` was replaced with `false` (same "real tokens"
+   semantics). It also had to include `mtmd-helper.h` explicitly, because the newer
+   `server-common.h` re-exports it and this one does not.
+
+## HIP / ROCm
+
+KVMem's GPU stage-in (`llama-kvmem-stagein.cu`, 1073 lines, 10 kernels) is
+CUDA-only, and there is **no host fallback implementation** — the adapter calls the
+26 `kvmem_stagein_*` symbols unconditionally, so a build without that translation
+unit fails to link.
+
+The CUDA surface actually used is tiny and hip-compatible: 25 host runtime entry
+points, `<<<>>>` launches, `__global__`, `blockIdx`/`threadIdx`/`blockDim`. No
+`__shfl_*`, no `atomicAdd`, no `__ldg`, no textures. So instead of forking the
+source, `src/adapter/llama-kvmem-cuda-compat.h` maps the CUDA names onto HIP.
+
+Two names have no HIP equivalent and are declared in the shim:
+
+| CUDA | HIP |
+|---|---|
+| `__nv_bfloat16` | `__hip_bfloat16` |
+| `half` | `__half` |
+
+`cudaPointerAttributes` maps to `hipPointerAttribute_t` (HIP spells it singular).
+
+Include sites routed through the shim: `llama-kvmem-stagein.cu`,
+`llama-kvmem-transfer.h`, `llama-memory-kvmem.cpp`, `llama-memory-kvmem-mtp.cpp`.
+
+## Building on this host
+
+Environment is the same as `F:\AI\llama-stack\scripts\build-prismml-fusion-hip.bat`.
+Three traps are worth knowing:
+
+1. **Do not call `enable_language(HIP)`.** On Windows `ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt`
+   sets `CXX_IS_HIPCC` unconditionally ("CMake on Windows doesn't support the HIP
+   language") and compiles `../ggml-cuda/*.cu` as **CXX** with the ROCm `clang++`,
+   which puts `.cu` files into HIP mode by extension. The stage-in follows the same
+   path. Enabling the HIP language instead makes CMake 4.2.3 write an unescaped
+   `HIP_PATH` into `CMakeHIPCompiler.cmake` (`Invalid character escape '\P'`), and
+   without a pre-set `CMAKE_HIP_ARCHITECTURES` it fails earlier with "Failed to find
+   a default HIP architecture".
+2. **`hip::host` / `hip::device` are directory-scoped IMPORTED targets.**
+   `ggml-hip` is a sibling of `src/`, so `src/CMakeLists.txt` has to repeat
+   `find_package(hip REQUIRED)`. `hip_DIR` is already cached, so it resolves instantly.
+3. **`lld-link.exe` and `lld.exe` are missing from `C:\Program Files\AMD\ROCm\7.1\bin\`**
+   (security software removes them; `ld.lld.exe` survives). LLD is a multi-call
+   binary, so copy `ld.lld.exe` to both names under
+   `F:\AI\llama-stack\temp_clean_later\toolchain\lld-compat\` and prepend that
+   directory to `PATH`. Without it any *new* `.cu` fails with
+   `unable to execute command: program not executable` / `amdgcn-link command failed`.
+   Existing object files mask the problem because ninja does not rebuild them.
+
+```bash
+# after exporting the ROCm/MSVC environment and the lld-compat PATH
+cmake -S <this tree> -B <this tree>/build-hip \
+      -DLLAMA_KVMEM=ON -DLLAMA_KVMEM_ROOT=<this tree>
+ninja -j 16 llama-server        # NOT `ninja all`
+ninja -j 16 llama-kvmem-server  # the one that can actually turn KVMem on
+```
+
+`kvmem/CMakeLists.txt` adds five test executables unconditionally, so `ninja all`
+will drag them in; build concrete targets instead.
+
+The whole thing is wrapped in `F:\AI\llama-stack\scripts\build-prismml-fusion-hip.bat`,
+which now also prepends the lld-compat directory and passes `-DLLAMA_KVMEM=ON`.
+
+## Status
+
+- Configure: green. `libkvmem` (static), the five adapter objects and
+  `llama-kvmem-stagein.cu.obj` are all in the ninja graph.
+- Compile: 10/10 kvmem objects, 0 errors, against the prism tree.
+- **`llama-server.exe`: links, `NINJA_RC=0`, 282/282 targets.**
+- **`llama-kvmem-server.exe`: links (1.86 MB).** Runs; `--help` prints the full
+  `--kvmem*` surface, so the adapter is reachable from the command line.
+- Device enumeration could not be checked in-sandbox: `--list-devices` reports
+  "no ROCm-capable device is detected" for the *pre-existing* `llama-server.exe`
+  and `llama-cli.exe` too, i.e. the sandbox has no GPU access. Must be re-checked
+  from the user's own terminal.
+
+## Not done
+
+- **`turbo3` / `turbo4` are not accepted as KV cache types by the KVMem tools.**
+  `kvmem_parse_cache_type()` (`tools/kvmem/kvmem-spec.cpp`) allows only
+  `f16|f32|q8_0|q5_0|q4_0`, and `kvmem_cache_types_ok()` gates quantized types to
+  `{q8_0, q5_0, q4_0}`. PrismML's TurboQuant cache types therefore cannot be
+  selected in the fused server, even though the kernel side would accept them:
+  `kvmem_cache_pack_rows()` falls through to `ggml_quantize_chunk()` for any
+  quantized type. Making this work needs (a) the two allow-lists extended and
+  (b) a check that the turbo block layout survives KVMem's
+  pack/unpack/`to_float` round trip. This is the open decision.
+- KVMem's lightweight web UI (`tools/kvmem/ui/`) is served from `--ui-dir`; the
+  bundled copy in `kvmem-webui.h` is what actually ships.
+- Five `kvmem_*_test` executables are defined by `kvmem/CMakeLists.txt` but are
+  not part of the normal build (`ninja all` would pull them in).
+- The non-Windows HIP path fails with an explicit `FATAL_ERROR`. It would need the
+  HIP language enabled at the project root.
+- `ggml/include/ggml-rpc.h` asserts `GGML_OP_COUNT == 101`. It was already stale at
+  102 before this work; bumping it means deciding an `RPC_PROTO_PATCH_VERSION` bump.
